{
 "about": "The one map of supplies: what every trade buys, and which trades supply it. The engine, the app and the server read it (the server's supply_trade_lines rows are generated from it). lines: id, name, group (Stock, Upkeep, Transport, Services; Bills are paid automatically and never shown as a supplier), category where the cost lands (cogs, oth, mkt, wages), suppliers (trade ids that supply it), local (supplier must be in the buyer's city to supply as an own company), lead and terms in days, critical (a short delivery cuts sales), variable (spend follows how busy the place is), noCapacity, delivered (spend is a share of delivered orders), auto (a bill), cargo (freight class). trades: per buying trade, the lines it needs: o is the share of the cost split (a cogs line's share of the cost of sales, 0 means it takes what the other cogs lines leave; an overhead line's share of the weekly fixed overhead), s is the share of sales an own company can take over, n a label for this buyer, from replaces the supplying trades for this buyer. Shares are game design values.",
